-- Collective + Emerging Coach + Pillar-3 content, 4-week seed (2026-07-19). Idempotent on phase='collective'.
delete from calendar_posts where phase='collective';
insert into calendar_posts (date, time, brand, platform, type, phase, title, caption) values ('2026-07-21','07:00','collective','linkedin','authority','collective',E'Collective · Broken Middle · held together with tape',E'You''re a great coach. The business around you is held together with tape.

A booking tool here. A payment link there. A spreadsheet for check-ins. A separate app for programs. None of it talks to each other, and all of it is your job at 9pm.

That''s not a you problem. It''s a structure problem, and it''s why most great coaches stay great coaches instead of real businesses.

There''s a better way to run the middle. More this week.');
insert into calendar_posts (date, time, brand, platform, type, phase, title, caption) values ('2026-07-23','07:00','collective','linkedin','authority','collective',E'Collective · Broken Middle · the busywork tax',E'Count the hours you spent coaching this week.

Now count the hours you spent on admin, tech, chasing payments, and rebuilding the same plan in three different tools.

The second number is the tax you pay for a business held together with tape. It''s invisible, it''s growing, and it''s the first thing that has to go if you want to scale without burning out.');
insert into calendar_posts (date, time, brand, platform, type, phase, title, caption) values ('2026-07-25','07:00','collective','linkedin','authority','collective',E'Collective · Own Don''t Rent · own a business',E'Most coaches are renting.

Renting their platform. Renting their software. Renting an audience on someone else''s terms. The day they stop paying, it disappears and they''ve built nothing that''s theirs.

The alternative isn''t building it all yourself from scratch. It''s running your own brand on an engine that''s already proven, so you own the business and skip the ten years of building the machine.');
insert into calendar_posts (date, time, brand, platform, type, phase, title, caption) values ('2026-07-28','07:00','collective','linkedin','authority','collective',E'Collective · Own Don''t Rent · still answers to you',E'''Powered by a proven engine'' scares some coaches. They think it means handing over their clients.

It''s the opposite. Your brand stays yours. Your clients are yours. Your voice, your prices, your relationships. The engine just does the heavy lifting underneath, so the work that used to eat your nights runs itself.

Powered by Body Recode. It still answers to you.');
insert into calendar_posts (date, time, brand, platform, type, phase, title, caption) values ('2026-07-30','07:00','collective','linkedin','authority','collective',E'Collective · One Standard · not a swapped template',E'A lot of ''coaching platforms'' are one template with the words swapped out. Strength language becomes yoga language becomes pilates language. Same engine, no understanding underneath.

That''s not what one standard means. It means the method reads your client''s actual state before it prescribes anything, in your modality, the way you would if you had unlimited time. Interpretation before prescription. That''s the line between a tool and a standard.');
insert into calendar_posts (date, time, brand, platform, type, phase, title, caption) values ('2026-08-01','07:00','collective','linkedin','authority','collective',E'Collective · Built in Public · what the engine does',E'Here''s what actually happens under the hood.

A client takes a scorecard. The engine reads it and names the state their body is in, and the pattern driving it. From that read it builds the plan, the nutrition, the check-in rhythm. The coach reviews, adjusts, and stays in control the whole way.

Read first. Prescribe second. Most tools skip step one. That''s the whole game.');
insert into calendar_posts (date, time, brand, platform, type, phase, title, caption) values ('2026-08-04','07:00','collective','linkedin','authority','collective',E'Collective · One Standard · collective not franchise',E'I could have made this a franchise. Sell as many licences as possible, take the fee, move on.

I didn''t, because a franchise mill optimises for volume and a collective optimises for standard. The value isn''t the software. It''s that every coach in it practises to one method, so the name means something. That only works if you stay small and curate hard.');
insert into calendar_posts (date, time, brand, platform, type, phase, title, caption) values ('2026-08-06','07:00','collective','linkedin','authority','collective',E'Collective · Built in Public · the pilot',E'The first coach onto the platform runs a yoga and meditation practice.

We built a whole modality for her, because yoga can''t just be strength coaching with the words changed. Her clients get a practice-readiness read, a plan in her voice, her brand start to finish. She gets to stop being the whole back office.

This is what pilot one looks like. Watching it live teaches me more than any plan.');
insert into calendar_posts (date, time, brand, platform, type, phase, title, caption) values ('2026-08-08','07:00','collective','linkedin','authority','collective',E'Collective · Founding Table · ten seats',E'I''m opening this to ten coaches. Not a hundred, not a waitlist of thousands. Ten.

Founding members get the system, founding terms locked for life, and a direct line to me while we build the standard together. When the ten are full, the door closes and the terms change.

If you''ve got a real method and an audience that already trusts you, the application is open. Link in comments.');
insert into calendar_posts (date, time, brand, platform, type, phase, title, caption) values ('2026-08-11','07:00','collective','linkedin','authority','collective',E'Collective · Built in Public · what I learned building it',E'I built the software that runs my own coaching business. No dev background.

The thing nobody tells you: designing the system forces you to understand your own business better than any course ever will. Every assumption gets exposed the moment you have to encode it.

That''s the real reason I can hand it to other coaches now. It isn''t a product I bought. It''s a business I understood, turned into an engine.');
insert into calendar_posts (date, time, brand, platform, type, phase, title, caption) values ('2026-08-13','07:00','collective','linkedin','authority','collective',E'Collective · Founding Table · who it''s for',E'Who the Collective is for: established coaches with a defined method and an audience that already listens, who are done running their business on tape.

Who it''s not for: people shopping for the cheapest tool, or coaches who want a generic template. The application screens for this on purpose, because one standard only holds if everyone in it belongs.

If that''s you, the door''s open for now.');
insert into calendar_posts (date, time, brand, platform, type, phase, title, caption) values ('2026-08-15','07:00','collective','linkedin','authority','collective',E'Collective · Founding Table · applications open',E'Applications for the founding ten are open.

It''s a two-minute fit scorecard, not a sales call. It tells you honestly whether the Collective is right for you and your practice right now, and if it is, we talk.

We only win when you win. That''s the whole model. Take the scorecard, link in comments.');
insert into calendar_posts (date, time, brand, platform, type, phase, title, caption) values ('2026-07-26','07:00','collective','linkedin','authority','collective',E'Emerging · one standard first',E'A note for the newer coaches watching this.

The founding ten is for established coaches, and that''s not you yet. That''s fine. The worst thing you can do early is bolt a big platform onto a practice that hasn''t found its method.

Learn to read before you prescribe. Build an audience that trusts one clear standard. Do that, and the platform will be waiting when you''re ready to grow into it.');
insert into calendar_posts (date, time, brand, platform, type, phase, title, caption) values ('2026-08-09','07:00','collective','linkedin','authority','collective',E'Emerging · grow into it',E'Every established coach was once a green one who didn''t know their method yet.

If you''re early, don''t try to buy your way past the reps. Get obsessed with one standard, apply it until it''s second nature, and let a real audience form around it. The infrastructure is the easy part, and it comes later.

When you''re ready to stop being the whole back office, there''ll be a lane for you.');
insert into calendar_posts (date, time, brand, platform, type, phase, title, caption) values ('2026-07-22','07:00','personal_brand','instagram','authority','collective',E'Personal · AI & LEVERAGE · engine to infrastructure',E'I built the engine to run my own coaching. Now other coaches run their practice on it.
Short one on what it means to turn your own business into infrastructure.

#kadedunstone #interpretbeforeyouact #buildinpublic #aicofounder #leverage');
insert into calendar_posts (date, time, brand, platform, type, phase, title, caption) values ('2026-07-29','07:00','personal_brand','instagram','authority','collective',E'Personal · AI & LEVERAGE · live case study',E'My own coaching business is the case study for the platform I license to other coaches.
Short one on why I''d never sell a system I don''t run myself.

#kadedunstone #interpretbeforeyouact #buildinpublic #aicofounder #leverage');
insert into calendar_posts (date, time, brand, platform, type, phase, title, caption) values ('2026-08-05','07:00','personal_brand','instagram','authority','collective',E'Personal · AI & LEVERAGE · one standard',E'A collective is only worth joining if everyone in it practises to one standard.
Short one on why the method, not the software, is the actual product.

#kadedunstone #interpretbeforeyouact #onestandard #coaching #leverage');
insert into calendar_posts (date, time, brand, platform, type, phase, title, caption) values ('2026-08-12','07:00','personal_brand','instagram','authority','collective',E'Personal · AI & LEVERAGE · others build on it',E'For years the engine ran one business. Mine. Now it runs other coaches'' businesses too.
Short one on the moment a tool you built becomes something others build on.

#kadedunstone #interpretbeforeyouact #buildinpublic #leverage #aicofounder');
